harvanvi language 
my idea is to see how the language work at atom leval so i created this 

flow 
Haryanvi Code → Lexer → Tokens → Parser → AST → Code Generator → JavaScript → Run

1️⃣ Haryanvi Code (Source Code)

This is the high-level code written by the programmer using Haryanvi keywords like ye and bol.
It is human-readable but not understandable by the computer directly.

2️⃣ Lexer (Lexical Analyzer)

The lexer reads the source code character by character and groups them into meaningful units called tokens.
It removes whitespace/comments and identifies keywords, identifiers, numbers, and operators.

3️⃣ Tokens

Tokens are the smallest meaningful units of a program, such as KEYWORD, IDENTIFIER, NUMBER, and OPERATOR.
They act as the input for the parser.

4️⃣ Parser (Syntax Analyzer)

The parser checks the grammatical structure of the token sequence according to language rules.
It organizes tokens into a structured format called an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST).

5️⃣ AST (Abstract Syntax Tree)

AST is a tree representation of program logic, not syntax.
It shows what the program does, ignoring formatting and unnecessary symbols.

6️⃣ Code Generator

The code generator traverses the AST and converts it into target code (here, JavaScript).
It maps high-level constructs to equivalent low-level instructions.

7️⃣ JavaScript Code

This is the generated executable code in JavaScript syntax.
It performs the same logic as the original Haryanvi program.

8️⃣ Run (Execution)

The generated JavaScript code is executed by the JS runtime (Node.js).
The final output is produced and shown to the user.

just download and run using command
node run.js 